{%- comment -%}
  fye-wishlist-button — the heart. Markup only; NOT WIRED UP YET.

  Added 31/08/2026. The real wishlist is its own session: live runs the T4S app
  wishlist (t4s_wis_cp, interactable.min.js, templates/search.wishlist.liquid)
  with fye-wishlist-share layered on top, and v3 carries none of it.

  This exists so the product page is visually complete and so there is exactly
  ONE place to wire when the store behind it is built — the same button will go
  on product cards, which is why it is a snippet and not inline markup.

  It is a real <button> with `aria-pressed`, not a link or a div, so the
  pressed state is already correct for a toggle once JS arrives. Until then it
  does nothing on click. That is deliberate and visible in the DOM
  (data-fye-wishlist has no handler) rather than hidden behind a dead href.

  Parameters:
    product — required for the id the eventual store will key on
    label   — override the default wording
{%- endcomment -%}
<button class="wish"
        type="button"
        data-fye-wishlist="{{ product.id }}"
        aria-pressed="false">
  {%- render 'icon', name: 'heart', class: 'icon--sm' -%}
  <span>{{ label | default: 'Add to wishlist' }}</span>
</button>
